feat: support Project and Activity object types for PM classification workflow

## Summary

Added support for `ObjectType` in PM classification input parameters.

The workflow now supports classification creation from both Project and Activity extended attributes:

- `ObjectType: Project` reads the EA value from `/api/projects/{projectId}`
- `ObjectType: Activity` reads the EA value from `/api/activities/{activityId}`
- Missing `ObjectType` defaults to `Project` to maintain backward compatibility

## Changes

- Added `ObjectType` parsing in `InputParameterParser`
- Added `objectType` to normalized input parameter model
- Added Activity details service to fetch activity extended attributes
- Updated PM classification processing to:
  - detect Activity input parameters
  - fetch activity details only when required
  - use project/activity extended attributes based on `objectType`
- Added logging to show:
  - where InputParameters were resolved from
  - resolved input parameter count and mapping
  - whether Activity data was required/fetched
- Updated affected test cases for new `objectType` field
- Merged latest `development` into the feature branch and resolved compatibility checks

## Behavior

Existing Project-based flow remains backward compatible.

Example:

```json
{
  "ExtAttrID": "44903",
  "ObjectType": "Activity",
  "ParentNamePath": "/DAM/Toolkit/Toolkit ID",
  "EstablishRelationship": "No"
}
